   "text": {
    "L1": "After the rain stops, the sun peeps through, and a rainbow may appear.",
    "L2": "The poem calls it a bridge of colours. This is a comparison, not a real bridge.",
    "L3": "A rainbow is curved across the sky from one side to the other, like a bridge.",
    "L4": "It has seven colours in a special order: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet.",
    "L5": "Say the colour names with rhythm, pausing at the ends of the lines.",
    "L6": "The rainbow is beautiful, but it will not stay. It fades away, so look up quickly.",
    "L7": "The poem celebrates beauty in nature, and words like fresh can describe what we see.",
    "L8": "Now put the seven colours in the order used in the poem."
   },
